    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4450" root="ثعل" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مَثْعَلَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A land in which are many</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَعَالِب</span>
[or <i>foxes</i>]; (S, K;) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْقَرَةٌ</span> meaning “ a land
in which are many <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَقَارِب</span> [or scorpions]; ” (S;)
as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُثَعْلِبَةٌ</span>. (K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثعلب</span>. [But see this
last word.])

